IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sgta-nouns`

-- Telecommunications Act 1999 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (TA1999.txt).
-- PART 3 ERECTION, MAINTENANCE AND REPAIR OF TELECOMMUNICATION INSTALLATIONS: ss 15 to 22.
-- Seat: the owner or occupier of the land or building the licensee wants to enter, and the licensee that must give notice and pay compensation.
-- 2000 Revised Edition numbers: s 15 was s 12, s 16 s 13, s 17 s 14, s 18 s 14A, s 19 s 15, s 20 s 16, s 21 s 17, s 22 s 18.

§ `s 15 Power to enter on and examine land other than State land`

-- src:1357 | 15.—(1) Whenever it appears to a public telecommunication
-- src:1358 | licensee that it is, or is probably, necessary to exercise the powers
-- src:1360 | Informal Consolidation – version in force from 2/10/2026
-- src:1361 | 2020 Ed. Telecommunications Act 1999 28
-- src:1363 | conferred by this Act upon a public telecommunication licensee in
-- src:1364 | respect of any land (other than State land) for the provision of any
-- src:1365 | telecommunication service or installation of any telecommunication
-- src:1366 | system, that licensee or any person authorised by that licensee in that
-- src:1367 | behalf may, after giving at least 3 hours’ previous notice to the
-- src:1368 | occupier of the land (if any) enter upon the land and may survey and
-- src:1369 | take levels and do all other necessary acts preparatory to the provision
-- src:1370 | of the service or installation of the system (as the case may be) so far
-- src:1371 | as the same may be possible without causing any damage or
-- src:1372 | disturbance.
@ref s 15(1) (src:1357-1372)
GIVEN `it appears to the public telecommunication licensee that it is, or is probably, necessary to exercise the powers conferred by the Act in respect of land (other than State land) for providing a telecommunication service or installing a telecommunication system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `hours of previous notice given to the occupier of the land, if any` IS A NUMBER
      `there is an occupier of the land` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the entry and acts can be done without causing damage or disturbance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 15(1): the licensee or its authorised person may enter the land and survey, take levels and do other necessary acts preparatory to the service or installation` MEANS
        `it appears to the public telecommunication licensee that it is, or is probably, necessary to exercise the powers conferred by the Act in respect of land (other than State land) for providing a telecommunication service or installing a telecommunication system`
    AND ((NOT `there is an occupier of the land`) OR (`hours of previous notice given to the occupier of the land, if any` AT LEAST 3))
    AND `the entry and acts can be done without causing damage or disturbance`

-- src:1376 | (2) In the event of any damage or disturbance being caused by
-- src:1377 | reason of the entry, the public telecommunication licensee must pay
-- src:1378 | compensation to the owner or occupier of the land.
@ref s 15(2) (src:1376-1378)
GIVEN `damage or disturbance was caused by reason of the entry` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 15(2): the public telecommunication licensee must pay compensation to the owner or occupier of the land` MEANS
    `damage or disturbance was caused by reason of the entry`

-- src:1380 | (3) Nothing in this section is deemed to authorise any employee or
-- src:1381 | agent of a public telecommunication licensee to cut down or clear
-- src:1382 | away any vegetation or any fence or other erection or to enter any
-- src:1383 | building or upon any enclosure attached to any building.
@ref s 15(3) (src:1380-1383)
GIVEN `the act is cutting down or clearing away vegetation or a fence or other erection, or entering a building or an enclosure attached to a building` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 15(3): section 15 authorises the employee or agent to do the act` MEANS
    NOT `the act is cutting down or clearing away vegetation or a fence or other erection, or entering a building or an enclosure attached to a building`

§ `s 16 Power to enter on State land for purposes of installation or plant`

-- src:1390 | 16.—(1) For the purpose of providing any telecommunication
-- src:1391 | service or installing any telecommunication system, a public
-- src:1392 | telecommunication licensee or any person authorised by the
-- src:1393 | Authority in that behalf may at any reasonable time —
-- src:1395 | (a) enter upon any State land;
-- src:1397 | (b) subject to the approval of the Authority and the Singapore
-- src:1398 | Land Authority, erect in or upon the State land such
-- src:1399 | installation or plant used for telecommunications or
-- src:1400 | excavate such trenches as may be necessary or proper
-- src:1401 | for the purpose of providing the service or installing the
-- src:1402 | system, as the case may be; and
-- src:1404 | (c) carry out all necessary works in connection therewith, and
-- src:1405 | may, in the course thereof, fell or lop trees, remove
-- src:1407 | Informal Consolidation – version in force from 2/10/2026
-- src:1408 | 29 Telecommunications Act 1999 2020 Ed.
-- src:1410 | vegetation and do all other things necessary for that
-- src:1411 | purpose.
@ref s 16(1) (src:1390-1411)
GIVEN `it is for the purpose of providing a telecommunication service or installing a telecommunication system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a public telecommunication licensee, or a person authorised by the Authority in that behalf` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is at a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 16(1)(a): the person may enter upon State land` MEANS
    `it is for the purpose of providing a telecommunication service or installing a telecommunication system` AND `the person is a public telecommunication licensee, or a person authorised by the Authority in that behalf` AND `it is at a reasonable time`

GIVEN `it is for the purpose of providing a telecommunication service or installing a telecommunication system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a public telecommunication licensee, or a person authorised by the Authority in that behalf` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is at a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority and the Singapore Land Authority approved the erection of installation or plant or the excavation of trenches` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 16(1)(b) and (c): the person may erect installation or plant or excavate trenches, carry out all necessary works, fell or lop trees and remove vegetation` MEANS
    `it is for the purpose of providing a telecommunication service or installing a telecommunication system` AND `the person is a public telecommunication licensee, or a person authorised by the Authority in that behalf` AND `it is at a reasonable time` AND `the Authority and the Singapore Land Authority approved the erection of installation or plant or the excavation of trenches`

-- src:1415 | (2) Where any such work interferes with improvements, buildings,
-- src:1416 | growing trees or crops, the licensee must pay compensation for any
-- src:1417 | damage or disturbance.
-- src:1419 | (3) Where the land is occupied under a licence for temporary
-- src:1420 | occupation, the compensation must be paid to the occupant under the
-- src:1421 | licence.
@ref s 16(2) and (3) (src:1415-1421)
GIVEN `the work interferes with improvements, buildings, growing trees or crops` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the land is occupied under a licence for temporary occupation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A STRING
`s 16(2) and (3): compensation for damage or disturbance is payable by the licensee to` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `the work interferes with improvements, buildings, growing trees or crops` THEN "no one under this subsection"
           IF `the land is occupied under a licence for temporary occupation` THEN "the occupant under the licence"
           OTHERWISE "the person who suffered the damage or disturbance"

§ `s 17 Power to enter on other land or building for purposes of installation or plant`

-- src:1428 | 17.—(1) Subject to this section, whenever it is necessary to do so
-- src:1429 | for the purposes of providing any telecommunication service or
-- src:1430 | installing any telecommunication system under this Act, a public
-- src:1431 | telecommunication licensee may under, upon or over any land (other
-- src:1432 | than State land) or in any building on any land —
-- src:1434 | (a) lay, place or carry on and erect such installation or plant
-- src:1435 | used for telecommunications as may be necessary or
-- src:1436 | proper for such purposes; and
-- src:1438 | (b) take such other action as may be necessary to render such
-- src:1439 | installation or plant safe and efficient,
-- src:1441 | and pay compensation to any person interested for any damage,
-- src:1442 | disturbance or disability that may be caused thereby.
@ref s 17(1) (src:1428-1442)
GIVEN `it is necessary for the purposes of providing a telecommunication service or installing a telecommunication system under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is laying, placing, carrying on or erecting installation or plant necessary or proper for such purposes, or taking other action necessary to render it safe and efficient` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee pays compensation to any person interested for any damage, disturbance or disability caused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 17(1): the public telecommunication licensee may do the act under, upon or over land (other than State land) or in a building` MEANS
    `it is necessary for the purposes of providing a telecommunication service or installing a telecommunication system under the Act` AND `the act is laying, placing, carrying on or erecting installation or plant necessary or proper for such purposes, or taking other action necessary to render it safe and efficient` AND `the licensee pays compensation to any person interested for any damage, disturbance or disability caused`

-- src:1446 | (2) Any compensation payable under subsection (1) may include an
-- src:1447 | annual payment for land, building or other immovable property used
-- src:1448 | for the purpose of the public telecommunication licensee’s
-- src:1449 | installation or plant.
@ref s 17(2) (src:1446-1449)
GIVEN `the compensation includes an annual payment for land, building or other immovable property used for the licensee's installation or plant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 17(2): the compensation payable under subsection (1) may include an annual payment` MEANS
    `the compensation includes an annual payment for land, building or other immovable property used for the licensee's installation or plant`

-- src:1453 | (3) A public telecommunication licensee does not acquire any right
-- src:1454 | other than that of user only in respect of any land, building or other
-- src:1455 | property under, over, along, across, in or upon which the licensee
-- src:1457 | Informal Consolidation – version in force from 2/10/2026
-- src:1458 | 2020 Ed. Telecommunications Act 1999 30
-- src:1460 | places any installation or plant used for telecommunications under
-- src:1461 | this section.
@ref s 17(3) (src:1453-1461)
GIVEN `the right is other than a right of user only in the land, building or other property` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 17(3): the public telecommunication licensee acquires the right` MEANS
    NOT `the right is other than a right of user only in the land, building or other property`

-- src:1465 | (4) Before entering on any land or building for the purpose
-- src:1466 | specified in subsection (1), a public telecommunication licensee
-- src:1467 | must give 14 days’ notice stating as fully and accurately as possible
-- src:1468 | the nature and extent of the acts intended to be done.
-- src:1470 | [10/2005]
-- src:1472 | (5) The notice must be given to the owner or occupier of the land or
-- src:1473 | building in the manner provided under this Act.
@ref s 17(4) and (5) (src:1465-1473)
GIVEN `days of notice given before entering` IS A NUMBER
      `the notice states as fully and accurately as possible the nature and extent of the acts intended to be done` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice is given to the owner or occupier of the land or building in the manner provided under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 17(4) and (5): the notice is as the licensee must give before entering` MEANS
    (`days of notice given before entering` AT LEAST 14) AND `the notice states as fully and accurately as possible the nature and extent of the acts intended to be done` AND `the notice is given to the owner or occupier of the land or building in the manner provided under the Act`

-- src:1477 | (6) The owner or occupier of the land or building may, within
-- src:1478 | 14 days after receiving the notice mentioned in subsection (4), lodge a
-- src:1479 | written objection with the Authority.
@ref s 17(6) (src:1477-1479)
GIVEN `days after receiving the notice` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 17(6): the owner or occupier may lodge a written objection with the Authority` MEANS
    `days after receiving the notice` AT MOST 14

-- src:1483 | (7) Where a written objection is lodged by the owner or occupier of
-- src:1484 | the land or building under subsection (6) (called in this section the
-- src:1485 | objector), the Authority must notify the public telecommunication
-- src:1486 | licensee concerned to resolve the dispute with the objector due to the
-- src:1487 | objection.
-- src:1489 | [30/2016]
-- src:1491 | (8) On receipt of the Authority’s notice under subsection (7), the
-- src:1492 | public telecommunication licensee must take genuine steps to resolve
-- src:1493 | the dispute with the objector due to the objection.
-- src:1495 | [30/2016]
@ref s 17(7) and (8) (src:1483-1495)
GIVEN `a written objection is lodged by the owner or occupier under subsection (6)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 17(7) and (8): the Authority must notify the licensee to resolve the dispute and the licensee must take genuine steps to resolve it` MEANS
    `a written objection is lodged by the owner or occupier under subsection (6)`

-- src:1497 | (9) If the public telecommunication licensee fails to resolve the
-- src:1498 | dispute due to the objection, the licensee must inform the Authority in
-- src:1499 | writing and also furnish all relevant information relating to the steps
-- src:1500 | taken by the licensee to resolve the dispute due to the objection.
-- src:1502 | [30/2016]
@ref s 17(9) (src:1497-1502)
GIVEN `the licensee fails to resolve the dispute due to the objection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 17(9): the licensee must inform the Authority in writing and furnish all relevant information relating to the steps taken` MEANS
    `the licensee fails to resolve the dispute due to the objection`

-- src:1504 | (10) After receipt of the information mentioned in subsection (9),
-- src:1505 | the Authority must notify the public telecommunication licensee and
-- src:1506 | the objector as to whether the Authority is satisfied that the licensee
-- src:1507 | has taken genuine steps to resolve the dispute due to the objection.
-- src:1509 | [30/2016]
@ref s 17(10) (src:1504-1509)
GIVEN `the Authority received the information mentioned in subsection (9)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 17(10): the Authority must notify the licensee and the objector whether it is satisfied that the licensee took genuine steps to resolve the dispute` MEANS
    `the Authority received the information mentioned in subsection (9)`

-- src:1514 | (11) The Authority must hold an inquiry (in such manner as the
-- src:1515 | Authority thinks fit) on the objection, giving each party a reasonable
-- src:1516 | opportunity to be heard if —
-- src:1518 | (a) the Authority notifies the parties under subsection (10) that
-- src:1519 | the Authority is satisfied that the licensee has taken
-- src:1520 | genuine steps to resolve the dispute due to the objection;
-- src:1521 | and
-- src:1523 | (b) the objection is not withdrawn.
@ref s 17(11) (src:1514-1523)
GIVEN `the Authority notified the parties under subsection (10) that it is satisfied that the licensee has taken genuine steps` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the objection is not withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 17(11): the Authority must hold an inquiry on the objection, giving each party a reasonable opportunity to be heard` MEANS
    `the Authority notified the parties under subsection (10) that it is satisfied that the licensee has taken genuine steps` AND `the objection is not withdrawn`

-- src:1527 | (12) Upon the conclusion of the inquiry, the Authority may
-- src:1528 | authorise, either unconditionally or subject to such terms,
-- src:1529 | conditions and stipulations as it thinks fit, any of the acts
-- src:1530 | mentioned in the notice given under subsection (4) to be carried out.
@ref s 17(12) (src:1527-1530)
GIVEN `the inquiry has concluded` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 17(12): the Authority may authorise, unconditionally or on such terms, conditions and stipulations as it thinks fit, any of the acts mentioned in the notice` MEANS
    `the inquiry has concluded`

-- src:1534 | (13) The public telecommunication licensee may enter the land or
-- src:1535 | building and do all or any of the acts mentioned in the notice given
-- src:1536 | under subsection (4) —
-- src:1538 | (a) where no written objection is lodged within the period
-- src:1539 | mentioned in subsection (6), after the expiry of that period;
-- src:1540 | or
-- src:1542 | (b) where a written objection is lodged under subsection (6) —
-- src:1544 | (i) after the objection is withdrawn;
-- src:1546 | (ii) after the public telecommunication licensee resolves
-- src:1547 | the dispute with the objector due to the objection; or
-- src:1549 | (iii) on the Authority’s authorisation under
-- src:1550 | subsection (12) subject to the terms, conditions and
-- src:1551 | stipulations imposed by the Authority under that
-- src:1552 | subsection.
@ref s 17(13) (src:1534-1552)
GIVEN `no written objection was lodged within the period mentioned in subsection (6), and the period has expired` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a written objection was lodged and has been withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a written objection was lodged and the licensee has resolved the dispute with the objector` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a written objection was lodged and the Authority has authorised the acts under subsection (12), and the licensee acts subject to the terms, conditions and stipulations imposed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 17(13): the public telecommunication licensee may enter the land or building and do the acts mentioned in the notice` MEANS
    `no written objection was lodged within the period mentioned in subsection (6), and the period has expired` OR `a written objection was lodged and has been withdrawn` OR `a written objection was lodged and the licensee has resolved the dispute with the objector` OR `a written objection was lodged and the Authority has authorised the acts under subsection (12), and the licensee acts subject to the terms, conditions and stipulations imposed`

§ `ss 18 to 22`

-- src:1559 | 18.—(1) Where a public telecommunication licensee (called in this
-- src:1560 | section the transferor licensee), after having laid, placed, carried on or
-- src:1561 | erected any installation or plant used for telecommunications under
-- src:1563 | Informal Consolidation – version in force from 2/10/2026
-- src:1564 | 2020 Ed. Telecommunications Act 1999 32
-- src:1566 | section 16 or 17, transfers the installation or plant, or any part of it, to
-- src:1567 | another public telecommunication licensee (called in this section the
-- src:1568 | transferee licensee), all rights conferred and obligations imposed on
-- src:1569 | the transferor licensee under this Act in respect of any land, building
-- src:1570 | or other property under, over, along, across, in or upon which the
-- src:1571 | transferred installation or plant (or part of it) has been laid, placed,
-- src:1572 | carried on or erected are deemed, on the transfer date, by virtue of this
-- src:1573 | subsection and without further assurance, to have been transferred to
-- src:1574 | the transferee licensee.
@ref s 18(1) (src:1559-1574)
GIVEN `the transferor licensee laid, placed, carried on or erected the installation or plant under section 16 or 17` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transferor licensee transfers the installation or plant, or part of it, to another public telecommunication licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 18(1): the rights conferred and obligations imposed on the transferor licensee in respect of the land, building or other property are deemed, on the transfer date, to have been transferred to the transferee licensee` MEANS
    `the transferor licensee laid, placed, carried on or erected the installation or plant under section 16 or 17` AND `the transferor licensee transfers the installation or plant, or part of it, to another public telecommunication licensee`

-- src:1578 | (2) Subsection (1) applies to every transfer of installation or plant
-- src:1579 | (or part of it) referred to in that subsection which takes place on or
-- src:1580 | after 1 July 2011.
@ref s 18(2) (src:1578-1580)
GIVEN `the transfer takes place on or after 1 July 2011` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 18(2): subsection (1) applies to the transfer` MEANS
    `the transfer takes place on or after 1 July 2011`

-- src:1588 | 19. Subsections (1) and (6) of section 17 do not —
-- src:1590 | (a) affect the right of a public telecommunication licensee to
-- src:1591 | enter into an agreement, commonly known as a wayleave
-- src:1592 | agreement, with the owner or occupier of any land for the
-- src:1593 | purpose of laying, placing, carrying or erecting any
-- src:1594 | installation or plant used for telecommunications on the
-- src:1595 | land;
-- src:1597 | (b) affect any such wayleave agreement subsisting
-- src:1598 | immediately before 1 December 1999; or
-- src:1600 | (c) affect the right of a public telecommunication licensee to
-- src:1601 | negotiate the use of land or facilities belonging to the State
-- src:1602 | or any other person.
@ref s 19 (src:1588-1602)
GIVEN `the matter is the right to enter into a wayleave agreement with the owner or occupier of land for laying, placing, carrying or erecting installation or plant, a wayleave agreement subsisting immediately before 1 December 1999, or the right to negotiate the use of land or facilities belonging to the State or any other person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 19: section 17(1) and (6) affect the matter` MEANS
    NOT `the matter is the right to enter into a wayleave agreement with the owner or occupier of land for laying, placing, carrying or erecting installation or plant, a wayleave agreement subsisting immediately before 1 December 1999, or the right to negotiate the use of land or facilities belonging to the State or any other person`

-- src:1608 | 20.—(1) Whenever it is necessary to do so for the purposes of
-- src:1609 | carrying out any functions and duties of the Authority under this Act
-- src:1610 | or any regulations made under this Act, the Authority may enter upon
-- src:1611 | any land or building, or stop or board any vessel, aircraft or vehicle
-- src:1613 | Informal Consolidation – version in force from 2/10/2026
-- src:1614 | 33 Telecommunications Act 1999 2020 Ed.
-- src:1616 | and may carry out all necessary inspections or investigations and do
-- src:1617 | all things necessary for such purpose.
@ref s 20(1) (src:1608-1617)
GIVEN `it is necessary for the purposes of carrying out the Authority's functions and duties under the Act or its regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 20(1): the Authority may enter upon any land or building, or stop or board any vessel, aircraft or vehicle, and carry out all necessary inspections or investigations` MEANS
    `it is necessary for the purposes of carrying out the Authority's functions and duties under the Act or its regulations`

-- src:1619 | (2) Whenever it is necessary to do so for the purpose of inspecting,
-- src:1620 | maintaining or repairing a public telecommunication licensee’s
-- src:1621 | installation or plant or for the purpose of carrying out any
-- src:1622 | functions conferred on a public telecommunication licensee under
-- src:1623 | this Act or under any licence granted under section 5, that licensee or
-- src:1624 | any person authorised by that licensee in that behalf may at any
-- src:1625 | reasonable time —
-- src:1627 | (a) enter upon any land or building, whether or not such
-- src:1628 | installation or plant has been laid, placed, carried or erected
-- src:1629 | on, under, upon or over the land or building; and
-- src:1631 | (b) carry out all necessary inspection, maintenance or repair,
-- src:1632 | and may in the course of that, fell or lop trees, remove
-- src:1633 | vegetation and do all other things necessary for the
-- src:1634 | purpose, causing as little damage as possible,
-- src:1636 | and pay compensation to any person adversely affected for any
-- src:1637 | damage that may be caused thereby for which compensation has not
-- src:1638 | already been assessed under section 17.
@ref s 20(2) (src:1619-1638)
GIVEN `it is necessary for inspecting, maintaining or repairing the licensee's installation or plant, or for carrying out functions conferred on the licensee under the Act or a licence granted under section 5` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is at a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the work causes as little damage as possible` IS A BOOLEAN
      `compensation is paid to any person adversely affected for damage for which compensation has not already been assessed under section 17` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 20(2): the licensee or its authorised person may enter upon the land or building and carry out inspection, maintenance or repair, felling or lopping trees and removing vegetation` MEANS
    `it is necessary for inspecting, maintaining or repairing the licensee's installation or plant, or for carrying out functions conferred on the licensee under the Act or a licence granted under section 5` AND `it is at a reasonable time` AND `the work causes as little damage as possible` AND `compensation is paid to any person adversely affected for damage for which compensation has not already been assessed under section 17`

-- src:1645 | 21.—(1) Where a public telecommunication licensee’s installation
-- src:1646 | or plant has been laid, placed, carried or erected in, on, over, under,
-- src:1647 | upon, along or across any land or building under section 16 or 17 (as
-- src:1648 | the case may be) and the owner or occupier of the land or building
-- src:1649 | desires to use the land or building in a manner which renders it
-- src:1650 | necessary or convenient for such installation or plant to be altered,
-- src:1651 | removed, relocated or diverted, the owner or occupier may request
-- src:1652 | the public telecommunication licensee to alter, remove, relocate or
-- src:1653 | divert such installation or plant accordingly.
@ref s 21(1) (src:1645-1653)
GIVEN `the installation or plant was laid, placed, carried or erected under section 16 or 17` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the owner or occupier desires to use the land or building in a manner which renders it necessary or convenient for the installation or plant to be altered, removed, relocated or diverted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 21(1): the owner or occupier may request the public telecommunication licensee to alter, remove, relocate or divert the installation or plant` MEANS
    `the installation or plant was laid, placed, carried or erected under section 16 or 17` AND `the owner or occupier desires to use the land or building in a manner which renders it necessary or convenient for the installation or plant to be altered, removed, relocated or diverted`

-- src:1657 | (2) The public telecommunication licensee must, at the request of
-- src:1658 | the owner or occupier of the land or building under subsection (1),
-- src:1659 | alter, remove, relocate or divert the installation or plant if it is
-- src:1661 | Informal Consolidation – version in force from 2/10/2026
-- src:1662 | 2020 Ed. Telecommunications Act 1999 34
-- src:1664 | satisfied that such alteration, removal, relocation or diversion is
-- src:1665 | reasonable and the owner or occupier complies with such reasonable
-- src:1666 | terms and conditions as the licensee may impose.
@ref s 21(2) (src:1657-1666)
GIVEN `the owner or occupier has requested under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee is satisfied that the alteration, removal, relocation or diversion is reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the owner or occupier complies with such reasonable terms and conditions as the licensee imposes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 21(2): the public telecommunication licensee must alter, remove, relocate or divert the installation or plant` MEANS
    `the owner or occupier has requested under subsection (1)` AND `the licensee is satisfied that the alteration, removal, relocation or diversion is reasonable` AND `the owner or occupier complies with such reasonable terms and conditions as the licensee imposes`

-- src:1670 | (3) The terms and conditions a public telecommunication licensee
-- src:1671 | may impose under subsection (2) may include terms and conditions
-- src:1672 | relating to the payment by the owner or occupier of the land or
-- src:1673 | building of all costs and expenses necessary for such alteration,
-- src:1674 | removal, relocation or diversion.
@ref s 21(3) (src:1670-1674)
GIVEN `the terms relate to the payment by the owner or occupier of all costs and expenses necessary for the alteration, removal, relocation or diversion` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 21(3): the terms and conditions the licensee may impose under subsection (2) may include this term` MEANS
    `the terms relate to the payment by the owner or occupier of all costs and expenses necessary for the alteration, removal, relocation or diversion`

-- src:1683 | 22.—(1) Where, in the opinion of a public telecommunication
-- src:1684 | licensee, there is at any time danger or suspected danger that any tree
-- src:1685 | (which term in this section includes undergrowth) near the licensee’s
-- src:1686 | installation or plant may interrupt or interfere with any
-- src:1687 | telecommunication service provided by the licensee or cause
-- src:1688 | damage to such installation or plant, the licensee may cause the
-- src:1689 | tree to be felled or dealt with in such other manner as will, in its
-- src:1690 | opinion, avert the danger.
@ref s 22(1) (src:1683-1690)
GIVEN `in the opinion of the licensee there is at any time danger or suspected danger that a tree (including undergrowth) near the licensee's installation or plant may interrupt or interfere with a telecommunication service provided by the licensee or cause damage to the installation or plant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 22(1): the licensee may cause the tree to be felled or dealt with in such other manner as will, in its opinion, avert the danger` MEANS
    `in the opinion of the licensee there is at any time danger or suspected danger that a tree (including undergrowth) near the licensee's installation or plant may interrupt or interfere with a telecommunication service provided by the licensee or cause damage to the installation or plant`

-- src:1694 | (2) A public telecommunication licensee is, in the exercise of its
-- src:1695 | powers under subsection (1), subject to the provisions of the Parks
-- src:1696 | and Trees Act 2005.
@ref s 22(2) (src:1694-1696)
GIVEN `the licensee exercises its powers under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 22(2): the licensee is subject to the Parks and Trees Act 2005` MEANS
    `the licensee exercises its powers under subsection (1)`

-- src:1698 | (3) Where a tree, which has been felled or otherwise dealt with
-- src:1699 | under subsection (1), was in existence before the public
-- src:1700 | telecommunication licensee’s installation or plant was placed,
-- src:1701 | erected or installed, the licensee may, subject to subsections (4)
-- src:1702 | and (5), pay to any person adversely affected such sum as may be
-- src:1703 | agreed by way of compensation.
@ref s 22(3) (src:1698-1703)
GIVEN `the tree was in existence before the licensee's installation or plant was placed, erected or installed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 22(3): the licensee may, subject to subsections (4) and (5), pay the person adversely affected such sum as may be agreed by way of compensation` MEANS
    `the tree was in existence before the licensee's installation or plant was placed, erected or installed`

-- src:1705 | (4) No further compensation shall be paid for the felling or lopping
-- src:1706 | of any tree or the clearing of any vegetation where the action is
-- src:1707 | necessary for the maintenance of a public telecommunication
-- src:1708 | licensee’s installation or plant and the tree and vegetation have
-- src:1710 | Informal Consolidation – version in force from 2/10/2026
-- src:1711 | 35 Telecommunications Act 1999 2020 Ed.
-- src:1713 | grown or been allowed to grow since the payment of compensation
-- src:1714 | under subsection (3).
@ref s 22(4) (src:1705-1714)
GIVEN `the action is necessary for the maintenance of the licensee's installation or plant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the tree and vegetation have grown or been allowed to grow since the payment of compensation under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 22(4): further compensation is payable for the felling or lopping of the tree or the clearing of the vegetation` MEANS
    NOT (`the action is necessary for the maintenance of the licensee's installation or plant` AND `the tree and vegetation have grown or been allowed to grow since the payment of compensation under subsection (3)`)

-- src:1716 | (5) No compensation is payable by a public telecommunication
-- src:1717 | licensee under subsection (3) in respect of any tree within 20 metres
-- src:1718 | of the centre line of any road constructed or maintained by the
-- src:1719 | Government or by any public authority unless it is proved that the tree
-- src:1720 | was in existence prior to the construction of the road.
@ref s 22(5) (src:1716-1720)
GIVEN `the tree is within 20 metres of the centre line of a road constructed or maintained by the Government or a public authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is proved that the tree was in existence prior to the construction of the road` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 22(5): compensation is payable by the licensee under subsection (3) in respect of the tree` MEANS
    (NOT `the tree is within 20 metres of the centre line of a road constructed or maintained by the Government or a public authority`) OR `it is proved that the tree was in existence prior to the construction of the road`

-- src:1722 | (6) Before the owner or occupier of any land fells, lops or clears any
-- src:1723 | tree or vegetation adjacent to a public telecommunication licensee’s
-- src:1724 | installation or plant, the owner or occupier must give the licensee
-- src:1725 | 14 days’ notice in writing of the intention to do so and must take all
-- src:1726 | such reasonable precautions as the licensee may require for the
-- src:1727 | protection of such installation or plant.
@ref s 22(6) (src:1722-1727)
GIVEN `days of notice in writing given to the licensee before felling, lopping or clearing` IS A NUMBER
      `the owner or occupier took all reasonable precautions the licensee required for the protection of the installation or plant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 22(6): the owner or occupier has done what the subsection requires before felling, lopping or clearing a tree or vegetation adjacent to the licensee's installation or plant` MEANS
    (`days of notice in writing given to the licensee before felling, lopping or clearing` AT LEAST 14) AND `the owner or occupier took all reasonable precautions the licensee required for the protection of the installation or plant`

-- src:1729 | (7) If any such owner or occupier fails to give notice as provided
-- src:1730 | under subsection (6) or having given notice fails to take any such
-- src:1731 | reasonable precautions as the public telecommunication licensee may
-- src:1732 | have required, the owner or occupier is liable to pay the licensee any
-- src:1733 | cost and expense incurred by the licensee for any damage caused to
-- src:1734 | any such installation or plant.
@ref s 22(7) (src:1729-1734)
GIVEN `the owner or occupier failed to give notice as provided under subsection (6), or having given notice failed to take the reasonable precautions the licensee required` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 22(7): the owner or occupier is liable to pay the licensee any cost and expense incurred for damage caused to the installation or plant` MEANS
    `the owner or occupier failed to give notice as provided under subsection (6), or having given notice failed to take the reasonable precautions the licensee required`

-- src:1736 | (8) A certificate purporting to be under the hand of the chief
-- src:1737 | executive of the licensee stating the amount of the cost and expense
-- src:1738 | incurred by the licensee under subsection (7) is prima facie evidence
-- src:1739 | of the amount due from the owner or occupier.
@ref s 22(8) (src:1736-1739)
GIVEN `a certificate purporting to be under the hand of the chief executive of the licensee states the amount of the cost and expense incurred under subsection (7)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 22(8): the certificate is prima facie evidence of the amount due from the owner or occupier` MEANS
    `a certificate purporting to be under the hand of the chief executive of the licensee states the amount of the cost and expense incurred under subsection (7)`

-- src:1741 | (9) If the amount due for the cost and expense is not paid within
-- src:1742 | 7 days after demand, the amount may be recovered in the same
-- src:1743 | manner as if it were a simple contract debt.
@ref s 22(9) (src:1741-1743)
GIVEN `days after demand that the amount is unpaid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 22(9): the amount may be recovered in the same manner as a simple contract debt` MEANS
    `days after demand that the amount is unpaid` GREATER THAN 7

-- src:1745 | (10) If any tree is felled or vegetation is cleared upon land adjacent
-- src:1746 | to a public telecommunication licensee’s installation or plant, it is
-- src:1747 | presumed until the contrary is proved that the tree was felled or the
-- src:1748 | vegetation was cleared by the owner or occupier of the land or by the
-- src:1749 | owner’s or occupier’s employees or agents acting as such.
@ref s 22(10) (src:1745-1749)
GIVEN `a tree is felled or vegetation is cleared upon land adjacent to the licensee's installation or plant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is proved that someone other than the owner or occupier, or their employees or agents acting as such, did it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 22(10): the tree was felled or the vegetation cleared by the owner or occupier of the land or by the owner's or occupier's employees or agents acting as such` MEANS
    `a tree is felled or vegetation is cleared upon land adjacent to the licensee's installation or plant` AND (NOT `it is proved that someone other than the owner or occupier, or their employees or agents acting as such, did it`)
